2.3.3 Financial Analysis Output Scope
The AI-generated Financial Analysis report will cover the following sections, aligned with the Natixis CPRM existing FA Format and Standards
#	FA Report Section	Content Description
1	Income Statement Review	Revenue performance analysis; profitability trends; segmental and regional breakdown; margin analysis; key year-on-year drivers
2	Balance Sheet Analysis	Asset composition and quality; liability structure; debt analysis including leverage ratios, and covenant considerations
3	Cash Flow Analysis	Operating ,financing cash flow trends; free cash flow generation; working capital changes etc.
________________________________________
2.3.4 Success Criteria — Financial Analysis
Success for the Financial Analysis component of the POC will be assessed across two dimensions:
Dimension 1 — Qualitative Assessment (Business Team Evaluation)
The CPRM Business Team will conduct a structured qualitative evaluation of AI-generated FA reports against human-produced baseline reports, assessing:
•	Analytical Depth: Does the report identify and articulate the key financial performance drivers at an appropriate level of detail?
•	Accuracy: Are the financial figures and trends referenced in the narrative consistent with source documents?
•	Structural Alignment: Does the report conform to the CPRM FA format, section structure, and expected level of coverage?
•	Tone and Style: Is the language and tone consistent with standard credit analyst practice?
•	Completeness: Are all five required analytical sections adequately covered?
Dimension 2 — Quantitative AI Metrics Evaluation
AI-generated outputs will be evaluated using the following formal metrics:
Metric	Description
Faithfulness	Degree to which generated content accurately reflects the content of the source documents without distortion
Additional Metrics	Context Precision , Context Recall (As per finalized architecture) 




High Level – TAD/Process Flow
