SECTION 1: ASSESSMENT METHODOLOGY
1.1 Overview
The evaluation framework measures the quality, accuracy, and reliability of AI-generated Financial Analysis (FA) reports across three core sections:
•	Profit & Loss (Income Statement) — P&L
•	Cash Flow Analysis
•	Balance Sheet Analysis
Each section is assessed independently through a Qualitative Assessment conducted by the CPRM Business Team, producing section-level scores combined into an Overall Achievement Score via weighted average. A separate Faithfulness Score is computed using an LLM-as-Judge framework to measure factual grounding against cited source documents.
________________________________________
1.2 Qualitative Assessment — Business Team Evaluation
The CPRM Business Team evaluates AI-generated FA sections against the standard of a human-produced Credit Memo, scoring across five criteria:
#	Criterion	Description	Weight
1	Analytical Depth	Quality and depth of financial driver identification and articulation	15%
2	Accuracy	Consistency of figures, ratios, and trends with source documents	50%
3	Structural Alignment	Conformity to CPRM Credit Memo format and section structure	10%
4	Tone and Style	Alignment with standard credit analyst language and conventions	10%
5	Completeness	Coverage of all required analytical sub-components per section	15%
	Total		100%
The Overall Achievement Score is the weighted average of these five criteria, reported as a percentage (0–100%) and tracked across iterations.
Scoring Scale
Score Range	Performance Level
0% – 20%	Poor
21% – 40%	Below Expectations
41% – 60%	Developing
61% – 80%	Good
81% – 100%	Excellent
________________________________________
1.3 Faithfulness Assessment — LLM-as-Judge Framework
The Faithfulness Score provides an automated, objective measure of factual grounding in AI-generated outputs, answering:
"Are the facts and claims in the AI-generated report supported by and traceable to the cited source documents?"
Methodology
Step	Activity
Step 1 — Claim Extraction	LLM judge extracts all discrete factual claims from the generated FA report
Step 2 — Source Retrieval	Cited source documents and passages are retrieved for each claim
Step 3 — Claim Validation	Each claim is validated as: Supported, Partially Supported, or Unsupported / Hallucinated
Step 4 — Score Computation	Faithfulness Score = proportion of Supported claims out of total claims extracted
Score Interpretation
Faithfulness Score	Interpretation
≥ 85%	High Faithfulness — outputs well grounded
70% – 84%	Moderate — acceptable; retrieval refinement recommended
50% – 69%	Low — significant grounding gaps; prompt improvements required
< 50%	Critical — high hallucination risk; not suitable for business review
