________________________________________

3.2 Key Observations
Observation	Detail
LLM Upgrades Drive Significant Gains	Each LLM upgrade (Gemma3 → Gemini → GPT 4.1 → GPT 5.5) delivered measurable quality improvements, confirming LLM capability as a primary quality driver
Scope Expansion Causes Temporary Regression	Adding CF & BS in Iteration 3 temporarily reduced P&L scores — a recognized trade-off during rapid scope expansion
Agentic Architecture is the Key Quality Enabler	The largest single-iteration gain came from transitioning to a fully agentic architecture in Iteration 4
Over-Decomposition Risks Coherence	Iteration 6's consolidation of multiple agents into one Sr. Credit Analyst addresses the analytical fragmentation risk of highly decomposed agent architectures
Hallucination Concentration Pattern	Unsupported claims tend to concentrate in inference-heavy sections (e.g., liquidity outlook, forward-looking commentary) rather than retrospective financial data sections
